{
 "title": "Why the Pythagorean Theorem Works",
 "lang": "en",
 "steps": [
  {
   "title": "The Right Triangle",
   "say": "Let's start with a right-angled triangle. It has two shorter legs, a and b, and the longest side opposite the right angle, called the hypotenuse, c.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "main_title",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 50,
     "text": "Why does a² + b² = c² work?",
     "size": 56,
     "anchor": "middle",
     "underline": true
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "tri1",
     "d": "M 100 500 L 100 260 L 280 500 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 5,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "rt_angle",
     "d": "M 100 475 L 125 475 L 125 500",
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 3
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_a",
     "x": 70,
     "y": 360,
     "text": "a",
     "size": 40,
     "color": "blue",
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_b",
     "x": 190,
     "y": 515,
     "text": "b",
     "size": 40,
     "color": "blue",
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_c",
     "x": 210,
     "y": 350,
     "text": "c",
     "size": 40,
     "color": "red",
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Build a Big Square",
   "say": "To see why the theorem works without heavy algebra, let's make a large square whose side length is a plus b.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "sq1",
     "x": 420,
     "y": 220,
     "w": 420,
     "h": 420,
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "s1_top_a",
     "x": 540,
     "y": 175,
     "text": "a",
     "size": 34,
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "s1_top_b",
     "x": 750,
     "y": 175,
     "text": "b",
     "size": 34,
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "s1_left_b",
     "x": 390,
     "y": 290,
     "text": "b",
     "size": 34,
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "s1_left_a",
     "x": 390,
     "y": 500,
     "text": "a",
     "size": 34,
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Place Four Triangles Inside",
   "say": "Now, let's place four identical copies of our blue right triangle inside the corners of this big square.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "s1_t1",
     "d": "M 420 220 L 660 220 L 420 400 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "s1_t2",
     "d": "M 660 220 L 840 220 L 840 460 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "s1_t3",
     "d": "M 840 460 L 840 640 L 600 640 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "s1_t4",
     "d": "M 600 640 L 420 640 L 420 400 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "blue"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "The Empty Space is c²",
   "say": "Look at the tilted empty space in the middle. Each side is the hypotenuse c, and the angles are 90 degrees, so its area is exactly c squared!",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "s1_c2",
     "d": "M 660 220 L 840 460 L 600 640 L 420 400 Z",
     "color": "red",
     "width": 5,
     "fill": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_c_side",
     "x": 730,
     "y": 340,
     "text": "c",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "red",
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_c2",
     "x": 630,
     "y": 410,
     "text": "c²",
     "size": 52,
     "color": "red",
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "cap1",
     "x": 630,
     "y": 670,
     "text": "Empty Area = c²",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "red",
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Rearrange the Triangles",
   "say": "Let's make an identical big square right next to it, and put the exact same four blue triangles inside—just slid together into two rectangles.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "sq2",
     "x": 1020,
     "y": 220,
     "w": 420,
     "h": 420,
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "s2_top_a",
     "x": 1140,
     "y": 175,
     "text": "a",
     "size": 34,
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "s2_top_b",
     "x": 1350,
     "y": 175,
     "text": "b",
     "size": 34,
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "s2_left_a",
     "x": 990,
     "y": 320,
     "text": "a",
     "size": 34,
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "s2_left_b",
     "x": 990,
     "y": 530,
     "text": "b",
     "size": 34,
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "s2_t1",
     "d": "M 1260 220 L 1440 220 L 1260 460 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "s2_t2",
     "d": "M 1440 220 L 1440 460 L 1260 460 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "s2_t3",
     "d": "M 1020 460 L 1260 460 L 1020 640 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "path",
     "id": "s2_t4",
     "d": "M 1260 460 L 1260 640 L 1020 640 Z",
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "blue"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Two New Empty Squares: a² and b²",
   "say": "Now the empty space is split into two smaller squares! The top-left one is a by a, and the bottom-right one is b by b.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "s2_a2",
     "x": 1020,
     "y": 220,
     "w": 240,
     "h": 240,
     "color": "green",
     "width": 5,
     "fill": "green"
    },
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "s2_b2",
     "x": 1260,
     "y": 460,
     "w": 180,
     "h": 180,
     "color": "green",
     "width": 5,
     "fill": "green"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_a2",
     "x": 1140,
     "y": 320,
     "text": "a²",
     "size": 52,
     "color": "green",
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_b2",
     "x": 1350,
     "y": 530,
     "text": "b²",
     "size": 52,
     "color": "green",
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "cap2",
     "x": 1230,
     "y": 670,
     "text": "Empty Area = a² + b²",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "green",
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Conclusion",
   "say": "Since both big squares are the exact same size and contain the exact same four blue triangles, their remaining empty areas must be equal!",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "eq_arrow",
     "x1": 860,
     "y1": 430,
     "x2": 960,
     "y2": 430,
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 5,
     "arrow": "both"
    },
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "final_box",
     "x": 450,
     "y": 750,
     "w": 700,
     "h": 100,
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "gray"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "final_eq",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 775,
     "text": "Therefore:  a² + b² = c²",
     "size": 48,
     "color": "ink",
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}